update progressnotedetail set updatedon = now(), updatedby = 'CDM-10132',

description = '<p>Safety &amp; Well-being</p><p>This worker completed a monthly virtual visit with Samya Gilbert along with paternal cousin, Teresa Wright-Gorham. <span style="color: rgb(62, 65, 69);">Ms. Wright-Gorham was asked the following questions: Have you or anyone in this house had a fever, cough, shortness of breath, nausea, vomiting, or diarrhea; Is currently sick with COVID-19 or the flu; or Has been told by a health provider that they should not have visitors due to illness? She answered no to all the questions.&nbsp;During the visit, Ms. Wright-Gorham reported that Samya is currently on punishment due to her lack of focus on her education. </span>Samya appeared to be safe and healthy. However, she was not in a good mood. She expressed not understanding why she was still punished and was advised by this worker to ask Ms. Wright-Gorham the reason and what she needs to see in order for her to be taken off. Ms. Wright-Gorham answered her questions and explained her expectations. Samya understood and said she would do better.</p><p><br></p><p>Mental &amp; Physical Health</p><p>Samya appears to be in good health and is up to date with all her routine appointments. Additionally, documentation is still pending from her vision appointment which Ms. Wright-Gorham is working on retrieving. Samya has been referred to Families First Counseling &amp; Psychiatry for mental health services. She completed her intake on Friday. She is waiting to be assigned a therapist. This worker advised Ms. Wright-Gorham to make sure a psychiatrist appointment is scheduled as Samya reported having difficulties going to sleep at night.</p><p><br></p><p>Progress towards Permanency Goal</p><p>Samya was found CINA on November 6, 2020. A permanency plan of Custody and Guardianship is being pursued. The Department received a call from mother, Ronnice Egerton on January 13, 2021 and expressed that she is interested in reunifying with Samya. Father, Samuel Gilbert, is currently incarcerated. The Guardianship packet has been provided to paternal cousin, Teresa Wright-Gorham. Samya continues to remain in contact with her father. In reference to her mother, Ms. Wright-Gorham reported that she had to block communication with Ms. Edgerton as the conversation she was having with Samya was more negative than positive. This worker has submitted a referral for a Family Support Worker to coordinate and supervise visits between Samya and her mother.</p><p><br></p><p>Housing or Placement</p><p>Samya continues to be placed with her paternal great-grandmother, Corrine Gilbert and paternal cousin, Teresa Wright-Gorham in Largo, Maryland. The home also includes Ms. Wright-Gorham''s 15-year-old daughter who shares a room with Samya and her adult son. Ms. Wright-Gorham reports no concerns other than Samya''s recent challenges with school.</p><p><br></p><p>Corrine Gilbert, Teresa Wright-Gorham, April Stringfield, and Taivonne Mathews-Wright were scheduled to be fingerprinted on January 12, 2021 and January 14, 2021 but had to be cancelled due to exposure of COVID-19. Ms. Wright-Gorham''s household has been rescheduled to February 4, 2021 and Ms. Stringfield goes on the February 8, 2021.</p><p><br></p><p>Employment &amp; Education</p><p>Samya is in the 5th&nbsp;grade and enrolled at Judge Sylvania W Woods, Sr. Elementary School. She continues to participate in Distance Learning due to COVID-19. Ms. Wright-Gorham reported that Samya has been taking school as a joke. She has been trying to give her monitored responsibility, but she is finding out that if she is not on her, Samya loses motivation and focus. Samya then gets mad when she gets on her or makes it everyone else''s fault.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Benchmarks and Life Skills (Youth 14 and Older)</p><p>N/A</p><p><br></p><p>If the youth identifies as LGBTQ, are they receiving supportive services around their sexual orientation and/or gender identity.</p><p>N/A</p><p><br></p><p>If the youth is pregnant or parenting, are they receiving supportive services? (If yes, list the services within the agency or community)</p><p>N/A</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>If the youth has history of sex trafficking/exploitation, are they receiving supportive services? (If yes, list the services within the agency or community)</p><p>N/A</p><p><br></p><p>Supportive Adults</p><p>Samya''s supports are her father and paternal family.</p>'

where progressnotedetailid = '05507700-9e71-4032-8502-e4141f96d9b2';